The origin of the OpenSVC AI agent, such as https://ai.opensvc.com:8090,
which the listener relays /api/ai/ to, so that om3-webapp reaches the agent
from its own origin, without CORS. Set it in the cluster configuration, to
the address of the agent that every node reaches, such as the name of its
VIP: the listener of any node relays to it.

The listener checks the certificate of the agent against the authorities of
the system, for a public certificate, and those of the cluster, the cluster
`ca` and `ca_sec_paths`, for a certificate a sec signed with the cluster CA.

The listener accepts there the OpenID tokens only, and passes each
unchanged, with the cluster id in X-OpenSVC-Cluster-ID: the agent verifies
the token again, through om3-mcp, against the issuer and the audience of
its own catalogue, and a token the agent refuses is answered 502
ai_token_rejected, the catalogue to check. The agent, not the listener,
ends a run at the expiry of its token.

Empty, /api/ai/ answers 404, and om3-webapp offers no assistant. The webapp
asks once per sign-in whether the cluster has an agent: one set, or removed,
while a user is signed in shows in the webapp of that user at their next
sign-in.
